language 0.1.0
module reliability
  means
    The ability of a system to preserve its required behaviour in the presence
    of faults, erroneous states and failures, and to restore that behaviour.

entity fault : thing
  means
    fault: a primary cause capable of bringing a system into an incorrect
    internal state.

entity error : thing
  means
    error: an internal state of a system that may lead to an observable
    failure.

entity failure : thing
  means
    failure: an observable deviation of the behaviour a system provides from
    the behaviour required of it.

entity recovery : thing
  means
    recovery: the process of returning a system from a failure or an erroneous
    state to an admissible state.

entity retry-policy : thing
  means
    retry policy: the rules for repeating an operation that did not succeed.

entity timeout : thing
  means
    timeout: the greatest admissible duration of waiting for an operation or
    an event to complete.

entity circuit-breaker : thing
  means
    circuit breaker: a mechanism that temporarily stops requests to a
    dependent component once a given level of failure is detected.

entity redundancy : thing
  means
    redundancy: the presence of additional interchangeable means of performing
    a function after part of the means is lost.

entity degradation : thing
  means
    degradation: an intended reduction of functionality or quality that
    preserves part of the useful behaviour.
